# Security Best Practices

## Secrets & settings

- Never commit API keys, Partner Center secrets, or tokens
- AI provider keys and LSP config belong in user settings under `%APPDATA%/XPad/`, not in the repo
- `.env` Store helper vars (`PFN`, `SID`, `STORE_ID`, `URL`) stay local; do not paste secrets into chat or logs

## File & path safety

- Treat paths from CLI, Open Folder, and find-in-folder as untrusted input
- Respect workspace excludes (`.git`, `node_modules`, `bin`, `obj`, `.vs`) when walking disks
- Honor read-only file attributes and the in-app RO toggle
- Large-file path: skip heavy features above 8 MB (`LargeFilePolicy`)

## Process & shell

- Embedded ConPTY terminal runs user commands — do not auto-execute untrusted content from documents
- Format-on-save / `FormatCommand` substitutes `$FILE` — keep command strings user-controlled via settings, not remote content
- Single-instance named pipe: only accept local handoff of file paths as designed

## Logging

- Crash log: `%APPDATA%/XPad/crash.log` — no API keys, tokens, or full document bodies
- AI debug dock may show provider traffic in debug mode — keep it opt-in

## Dependencies & shipping

- Prefer `dotnet` restore with lock/consistent package versions from the csproj
- MSIX / Store / GitHub Releases: unsigned Store submit only via CI secrets; skip GitHub updater for Store installs (`PackageIdentity`)
- Audit Avalonia / AvaloniaEdit / TextMate updates for regressions before release

## Checklist before release

- [ ] No secrets in repo or release notes
- [ ] `dotnet test` green
- [ ] Smoke CLI / single-instance / workspace as needed
- [ ] Version bump via `scripts/release.ps1` (or intentional dry-run)

